# ETK RADIO -- the fast rung: the interactive RADIO CHECK, and the fallback (spec 4/5).
#
#   ollama create etk-radio:4b -f tools/radio/Modelfile.fast
#
# qwen3.5:4b answers the pad-menu questions the operator presses on the couch ("why did it
# crash?", "is arm B ahead yet?") behind a _ProgressCard that shows elapsed time. It is
# ~40% faster than the 9b and, on the credential exam, scored identically after
# adjudication and never flapped across three seeds -- so it is also the honest
# single-model fallback if the node is ever halved (spec 12). With
# OLLAMA_MAX_LOADED_MODELS=1 every 4b<->9b switch costs a reload; Phase 1 measures whether
# the split earns it.
#
# NO `SYSTEM` LINE HERE, DELIBERATELY -- same reason as Modelfile.debrief: the service
# sends prompts/engineer.md as the system message of every call so that `prompt_sha256`
# is hashed over the bytes the model actually received, and so a `git pull` on the node
# refreshes the doctrine without an `ollama create`.
#
# THINKING IS OFF, and the Modelfile cannot say so: the service passes `"think": false`
# in the /api/chat body. This rung is the one that most needs it -- a 4B on this node
# spent 2,766 tokens deliberating over a two-sentence question.

FROM qwen3.5:4b

PARAMETER temperature 0.2

PARAMETER num_ctx 8192

# Shorter than the debrief rung on purpose: a radio check is one answer to one question
# with the operator sitting there watching a timer, not a full debrief.
PARAMETER num_predict 400
